## Frontend Architecture

### Feature Module Pattern

```
src/features/<domain>/
├── api.js     # API calls (uses shared apiClient)
└── store.js   # Zustand store (optional)
```

### Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/proxy.js` | Next.js 16 middleware — auth gate (cookie check) |
| `src/lib/apiClient.js` | Axios instance (`withCredentials: true`, base URL) |
| `src/lib/cn.js` | `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` utility |
| `src/lib/ui.js` | UI component catalog (`statSurface`, `btn.*`, `card*`, `input`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) |
| `src/components/ui/` | Design system primitives (`Button`, `Card`, `Input`, `PasswordInput`, `Select`, `Textarea`, `Label`, `Modal`, `StatusBadge`, `PageLoader`) |
| `src/components/ProtectedRoutes.jsx` | Client-side route guard |
| `src/components/Providers.jsx` | Context wrapper (TanStack Query, theme, etc.) |
| `src/schemas/fields.js` | Shared Zod field validators |

### Views Layer

- `app/` pages are thin wrappers that render `views/<Role>/` components
- Route groups: `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`, `(exam)`

### State Management

- **Server state**: TanStack Query (all data fetching/caching)
- **Client state**: Zustand (auth user, theme, assessment-taking state, UI state)
- **Forms**: react-hook-form + Zod resolver with shared UI primitives

### Tailwind v4 & Modern Web Standards

- No `tailwind.config.js` — CSS-first config in `globals.css`
- `@theme inline {}` block with semantic color tokens
- Dark mode via `.dark` class on `<html>` (`color-scheme: light/dark` synced)
- `cn()` utility for class merging
- **Typography (`improve-text-layout-and-legibility`)**: `text-wrap: balance` on headings ($\le 6$ lines); `text-wrap: pretty` on paragraphs.
- **Forms & A11y (`validate-input-after-interaction`, `accessible-error-announcement`)**: Use `:user-invalid` / `:user-valid` and sync with `aria-invalid` and `aria-errormessage`. Form controls must link error messages to input fields via `aria-errormessage`.
- **Password Policy**: 5-point standard ($\ge 8$ chars, uppercase, lowercase, number, special char `@$!%*?&`) with live visual requirement checklist.
- **Timers**: Question and exam countdowns use `role="timer"` and `tabular-nums` for rock-steady numeral layout in LTR and RTL.
- **Modals (`prevent-page-scroll-under-modal-dialog`)**: Pure CSS scroll containment via `overscroll-behavior: contain` on `<dialog>` and `::backdrop`; never lock body scroll with `overflow: hidden`.
- **Performance (`defer-rendering-heavy-content`)**: `content-visibility: auto` + `contain-intrinsic-size` on long question lists or heavy tables.

---

## Common Pitfalls

1. **Port 5005**: Fastify binds to port 5005 (PORT in `.env`, default `5005`). Only ONE backend PM2 process should bind this port. Never reference port 8000.
2. **PM2 reload after build**: When running local dev/e2e with Next.js under PM2, run `npx pm2 restart all` after `npm run build` to load new Turbopack chunk manifests.
3. **EADDRINUSE**: `pm2 delete <duplicate>` then `pm2 restart <name>`.
4. **Config cache**: DB changes take 60s to reflect; restart PM2 for immediate effect.
5. **SKIP_CAPTCHA**: Set `true` when no reCAPTCHA is configured.
6. **FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID**: Must be set in backend `.env` for Google Auth to work.
7. **Groq models**: Use current catalog (`openai/gpt-oss-120b`), not deprecated Llama models.
8. **Font paths**: Backend builds copy fonts from `src/assets/fonts/` to `dist/assets/fonts/`.
9. **Migration Parity**: When updating `src/db/schema.ts`, run `npm run db:generate` to keep SQL migrations in `drizzle/` perfectly in sync with Drizzle schema.
10. **Node version**: Server runs Node 24; use `npm install --ignore-engines` on deploy if required.
11. **Container Scale Jitter**: `cardInteractive` contains `active:scale-[0.99]`. Never wrap forms or container sections with it; reserve strictly for leaf clickable cards.
12. **Flash of Empty State (FOES)**: Always gate `<EmptyState />` with `hasLoaded` or `!loading`, rendering skeleton loaders during initial fetch.
13. **Dynamic Param Normalization**: In Next.js App Router dynamic routes, always normalize `const rawId = params?.id || params?.assessmentId; const id = Array.isArray(rawId) ? rawId[0] : rawId;`.
